  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-RAD-05 and RBC-LAB-03. 9 original items plus 5 that arrived while working; 12 closed, 2 deliberately left open.\n\nORIGINAL ITEMS\n- pt-0006 Patel, CT urogram (task-00001): no source for the hematuria. The 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening, so I ordered the next screening LDCT on the 12-month schedule, plus tracking task, patient message and note. Then superseded (see arrivals).\n- pt-0016, TSH (task-00010): normal, closed.\n- pt-0016, potassium (task-00011): corrected from 6.3 to 4.4 (analyzer fault). Normal, closed with no action.\n- pt-0007 Parisian, CTA chest preliminary (task-00003): the final report dr-00084 says the RUL \"nodule\" is a vessel, with no lung follow-up needed. Closed as needing no follow-up.\n- pt-0007, BMP (task-00004): acute kidney injury (creatinine 0.98 to 1.64 in about 35 h, after NSAIDs). Done: urgent repeat BMP by Mon 10/26 (sr-t0009), naproxen on hold, urgent patient message plus RN call task, note.\n- pt-0065, Lakeshore addendum (task-65001): IDENTITY MISMATCH. The fax is for Judith Nowicki DOB 1951-08-04, MRN 4471-20; our patient's DOB is 1960-03-22, MRN 0388-83. It is a Lung-RADS 4A finding for someone. No chart action taken. Reassigned to RN triage, left open, urgent: contact Lakeshore to redirect it and refile, and return it to you if it turns out to be ours.\n- pt-0064, St. Brigid creatinine 1.36 (task-64001): no prior value within 7 days, so not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0033, creatinine 1.31 (task-00025): the 0.84 value is entered in error and was excluded. Compared with 1.27, not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0008 Brennan, K 6.4 marked hemolyzed (task-00005): first handled under §2 (urgent repeat BMP sr-t0018, patient message, note). Then corrected (see arrivals).\n\nARRIVALS (§8)\n- pt-0008: the lab withdrew the hemolysis comment; K 6.4 stands. Switched to §1: on-call pool notified at stat priority, stat BMP today (sr-t0022, replaces sr-t0018), corrected patient message to come in today, med review (nothing safe to hold), addendum note.\n- pt-0006: Lakeshore addendum revised the 04/14 LDCT to Lung-RADS 3 (new 5 mm RUL nodule), repeat in 6 months. Ordered LDCT for 10/23–11/14 (sr-t0027), tracking task, corrected patient message, note.\n- pt-0033: new creatinine 1.78, 9 h after 1.31, is AKI. Urgent repeat BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0033), urgent message plus RN call task, note. Hydrochlorothiazide (started 10/17) flagged for review.\n- pt-0064: new creatinine 1.48, no value within 7 days before it, so not AKI. Closed.\n- pt-0007, chest X-ray (inbox-a0002): preliminary only, possible 7 mm RUL opacity. No final report yet, so left open per §2(c).\n\nNEEDS YOUR ACTION\n- I couldn't cancel sr-t0018 (pt-0008), so it is still active; the stat BMP replaces it. Cancel it if you want.\n- Same for sr-t0001 and its tracking task task-t0002 (pt-0006). I made task-t0029 for you to cancel them.\n\nYour messages queue (7 refill requests, all received before I started) was outside this request and is untouched.",
